On 2026-07-13 all 122 skills in `~/.claude/skills/` were audited and cleaned up:

- Rewritten descriptions: pp-recipe-goat, graphify (also renamed from `graphify-windows`), diagram-generator, pp-catapult-openfield-connect, pp-fireflies, web-scraping (narrowed to Exa; firecrawl suite owns scrape/crawl), everything-search, frontend-slides (absorbed slide-deck-generator's triggers + component library).
- Body rewritten: research-assistant (routing, save-path convention `research/<slug>-<date>.md`, non-blocking scope, hard cases).
- Trigger bugs fixed: fable-mode ("Nate"→"the user"), process-interviewer (bare "interview me" collided with the interview-me daily ritual).
- Deleted: `diagnose` (superseded by diagnosing-bugs), `slide-deck-generator` (merged into frontend-slides).
- Archived, not deleted: `FireFlies_to_Obsidian` → `~/.claude/skills-archive/` (contains unique Fireflies→Obsidian .py scripts; live job is done by meeting-sync).

**Why:** duplicate/colliding trigger descriptions made skill loading a lottery; several descriptions were truncated by a generator bug.
**How to apply:** removed-skill contents live in `~/.claude/skills-archive/`. Known remaining debt: graphify SKILL.md is 1,194 lines (should move step code to references/); 11 dead-weight candidates (8 firecrawl sales/marketing + 3 starter-* brand skills) kept pending Eric's call.

Third wave 2026-07-13 (bucket-taxonomy pass, same session as wave 1): built `claude-stack-doctor` (verification skill + scripts/stack-check.ps1 — checks the 3 scheduled tasks, 2 venvs, memsearch, flush pipeline; its first run caught the live KeystoneOS Morning failure → root cause: rg.exe missing from Task Scheduler PATH → fixed in KeystoneOS PR #2, branch worktree-fix-cadence-rg-path) and `html-to-pdf` (headless-Chrome utility, tested). Split improve-system's 5 modes: improve-system → vault Audit only; new `session-miner` (historical review) + `capture-insight` (experience capture); Skill Review folded into write-a-skill; Foundation retired to starter-* skills. process-interviewer now hands specs to write-a-skill instead of auto-building (also removed its dead references/skill-output-template.md pointer). Queued skill builds, in priority order: followup-chaser (orchestration), pp-vald (enrichment; VALD /tests pages by modifiedFromUtc gotcha), athlete-case-file (orchestration, depends on pp-vald), drive-janitor.

Second pass 2026-07-13 (same day, structural lens — scripts/assets/config/AskUserQuestion/argument-hint): full report at `~/.claude/skills-audit/structural-audit-2026-07-13.md`.

Fixes applied 2026-07-14 (Claude session, after Codex's third wave): all 7 broken skills repaired — session-handoff Nate-paths → %USERPROFILE%; pp-catapult 17 bare `catapult-pp-cli` → `catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli`; everything-search rewritten around `es.exe` (Everything GUI installed at `C:\Program Files (x86)\Everything\`, es.exe CLI needs one-time download — skill documents it); pbir-report-builder + decision-toolkit phantom-file sections replaced with honest self-contained instructions; five-slides-generator Steps 5–8 rewritten for Windows (scratch dir in $env:TEMP, PowerPoint COM slide-PNG QA since no LibreOffice, Desktop delivery) incl. reference templates. Also: interview-me stale slug → delegates to memory-write; fact-checker got a mandatory live-research step; roast Task→Agent; firecrawl dead links (firecrawl-cli → firecrawl, firecrawl-build hub → installed siblings); contribute-catalog three pin aligned to 0.181.2; **Codex's gate-appending pass had duplicated its sections in 8 files** (session-handoff, fact-checker, articulation-skill, design-academy-skill, diagram-generator, humanizer, research-assistant, starter-design-tokens, starter-voice-profile) — all deduped; argument-hint added to 29 skills (now 43/126; nested quotes break YAML frontmatter — graphify bit this).

Autonomous wave completed 2026-07-14 (5 parallel subagents, all verified): `_shared/config.json` created (vault paths + keystone block) and 15 skills pointed at it; graphify refactored 47KB→14KB SKILL.md + 16 py_compile-clean scripts/ + config.json + references/ + assets/extraction-prompt.md (NOTE: pip package is `graphifyy` (double-y) providing module `graphify` — intentional, not a typo); firecrawl 15 deliverable templates → assets/ + shared Failure Handling section + AskUserQuestion adapter note; meeting-sync got scripts/sync.py (ports KeystoneOS c5b1208 directory-diff export detection, atomic state writes, JSON stdout) + assets/meeting-header.md; name-meetings/fireflies-intake unattended-mode contract (HIGH-confidence auto-apply, rest → review[] array) + auth story aligned to real doctor JSON output (`auth: configured` — both old string checks were wrong); AskUserQuestion adopted in ~14 skills; hyperframes-cli capture/snapshot/publish documented with flags verified via `npx hyperframes@0.7.57 --help`.

Consolidation decisions executed 2026-07-14 (Eric pre-approved judgment calls; constraints: Pocock content as-written, plugin wins over local duplicates): 22 local folders archived to `~/.claude/skills-archive/pocock-local-2026-07-14/` — the 21 duplicates of mattpocock-skills plugin v1.2.0 (manifest registers 22 skills; only resolving-merge-conflicts had no local copy) plus to-issues (older subset of plugin's to-tickets). Skill count 126→104. Side effect: archiving local code-review un-shadowed the built-in /code-review. Note: local customizations (argument-hints, AskUserQuestion edits) on those 21 went to the archive with them — plugin versions are vanilla by design. Kept: to-prd (distinct "PRD" vocabulary, explicit-invoke only, no plugin equivalent), zoom-out, watch (not in plugin). Handoff triplication resolved by boundary, not deletion: closeout Step 4 = canonical durable handoff (docs/handoffs/); session-handoff = chat-only pre-/clear (boundary lines added to both); plugin handoff untouched. interview-me's weekly-synthesis mode removed — now defers to weekly-review by name.

Follow-up candidates: hyperframes-cli has ~12 more undocumented commands (check, beats, keyframes, grade-compare, compare, present, cloud, lambda, cloudrun, add, catalog, auth).
